From d3536ed21c47af11fc7d0a408cfa74bb08364918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Tammi <mikatammi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:30:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rts: don't restrict the RTS's static library dirs to libffi's

Since "Use libffi-clib" (0f53ccc6), rts.buildinfo sets

    extra-lib-dirs-static: @FFILibDir@

When configure is given --with-ffi-libraries, this list is non-empty,
and Cabal then no longer falls back to extra-lib-dirs for the static
library dirs (extraLibDirsStaticOrFallback in
Distribution.Simple.Register). The directories hadrian passes with
--extra-lib-dirs (for libnuma, libdw and libzstd) are then missing from
the RTS's library-dirs-static. Linking any executable then fails when
those libraries aren't on the linker's default search path, e.g. with
nixpkgs on x86_64-linux:

    ld.gold: error: cannot find -lelf
    ld.gold: error: cannot find -ldw
    ld.gold: error: cannot find -lnuma

GHC 9.14 doesn't set static library dirs for the RTS and isn't
affected. Drop the line, so the static library dirs fall back to
extra-lib-dirs again, which also contains libffi's directory.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
 rts/rts.buildinfo.in | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rts/rts.buildinfo.in b/rts/rts.buildinfo.in
index bb42c4e..1e62e08 100644
--- a/rts/rts.buildinfo.in
+++ b/rts/rts.buildinfo.in
@@ -2,4 +2,3 @@ extra-libraries: @EXTRA_LIBS@
 extra-libraries-static: @EXTRA_LIBS@
 include-dirs: @FFIIncludeDir@
 extra-lib-dirs: @FFILibDir@
-extra-lib-dirs-static: @FFILibDir@
